{"duration_api_ms":241025,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"05ada644-f996-4597-b253-a08fede15d8c","total_cost_usd":0.286352,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":23898,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17765},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11842,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23898,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11842,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11842},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":23898,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11842,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.286352,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17765,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 3 of 20 evaluated designs are feasible and 12 return no geometry. Every geometry failure has high bluntness_ratio combined with low cone_half_angle. Every valid geometry satisfies roughly (2*b - 0.1)*cos(theta) <= 0.86, and every failure is at or above 1.0. This is my own inference from the ids and the failure messages, not a stated rule. Feasible max_g is capped at 12 (C-1a25df448e6f sits at 11.99), and g rises with steeper flight_path_angle. Heat-shield mass fraction is roughly 1 - m ~ 0.09*D^2, so diameter must stay at or below about 3.2 m (C-c97855c2d790 at 4.27 m fails). The hypervolume is dominated by lowering bondline temperature, since the 300-450 K range is small. The current front point C-924ebfff660f is at 422 K and 363 kW/m2. Bluntness, diameter and flight-path angle are the levers still unexplored.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-924ebfff660f (D=2.81, b=0.72, theta=69.6, gamma=-2.43) is the only front point: q=362.8k, T=422.0, g=10.1.\",\"C-954afbe3d7da (b=0.396, theta=66.3, gamma=-1.79) has T=443 and q=418k. It is dominated by C-924ebfff660f, which has larger bluntness and a steeper angle, so higher bluntness and steeper entry lower T.\",\"C-1a25df448e6f (gamma=-3.88, theta=36.4, D=2.39) sits at g=11.99, essentially on the g limit. Steeper angles (C-02335773e828 at -6.0 gives g=15.9, C-2d91d8d713d7 at -7.4 gives g=19.2) are clearly infeasible.\",\"Steep, big-D designs reach low T but violate g: C-c97855c2d790 gives T=375, C-2d91d8d713d7 gives T=381 and C-02335773e828 gives T=394. Bondline temperature falls with a larger b*D^3*sin(gamma) product.\",\"Geometry failures: C-1fdb98d93248 (b=1.32, theta=63.9), C-0c229251fec4 (b=1.26, theta=59.1), C-f97de340f655 (b=0.79, theta=47). Valid: C-c76d29c9a126 (b=0.515, theta=22.8) and C-924ebfff660f (b=0.72, theta=69.6). Large theta allows larger b.\",\"Mass-fraction margins: 0.30 at D=2.81, 0.23 at D=2.92, 0.037 at D=3.22 (C-2d91d8d713d7), -0.83 at D=4.27.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This relies on prior Allen-Eggers-type scaling, calibrated to the data. Peak stagnation heat flux scales as sqrt(sin(gamma)/(Rn*CdA)), so it falls with larger nose radius and larger diameter. Heat load, and hence bondline temperature rise, scales roughly as (b*D^3*sin(gamma))^-0.5. A fit to eight evaluated points gives T-300 ~ 122*(X/1.218)^0.65, with X = (b*D^3*sin(gamma))^-0.5. Larger bluntness and diameter therefore lower both objectives at once, and a steeper angle lowers T at some cost in q and g. Peak g is set mainly by gamma and stays below 12 for |gamma| up to about 3.6-3.9 deg at large D. A high cone angle (about 70 deg) lets a very blunt nose (b about 1.1-1.3) stay geometrically valid, gives a low area-to-mass ratio, and keeps the shield mass fraction low. The plan is to push b up to about 1.1-1.3 at theta about 70, D up to about 3.0-3.2, and gamma to -3 to -3.8, while probing the g limit, the mass limit and the geometry boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The geometry boundary is inferred from 20 samples. My fit of the nose-radius factor was inconsistent (about 1.8-1.95 times b*D/2), so designs with b >= 1.25 at theta=70 could still be invalid. The g model is extrapolated for large D and high theta. The T and q predictions come from a power-law fit to 8 points and may be off by 10-20%. The mass-fraction margin near D=3.2-3.3 depends on shield area, which I estimate only roughly.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Increase bluntness and diameter at high cone angle to cut both heat flux and heat load, with a moderately steeper entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the bluntness and diameter increase gives the predicted sizeable drop in T and q.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Same shape as the previous proposal but steeper (-3.2 deg) to trade a little heat flux for lower bondline temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the gamma trade-off at fixed shape and checks that g stays below 12 at -3.2 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Push toward the predicted optimum: large D, b=1.2, and gamma=-3.5 close to the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":383,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Candidate for a big hypervolume gain via T around 383 K, and it tests the g and mass limits.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Most aggressive corner: D=3.2, b=1.25 and gamma=-3.8, which could push T to about 378 K.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":378,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g, mass and geometry limits at once. Bluntness index (2b-0.1)cos(theta) is about 0.82, so validity is uncertain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller diameter with a blunt nose and gamma=-3.0 to see how much diameter contributes.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":383000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills in the diameter dependence and gives a mid-range trade-off point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-954afbe3d7da\",\"rationale\":\"Large D, moderate theta=65 and b=0.9, which is geometrically safe. Checks whether a lower cone angle is acceptable.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the mass-fraction limit near D=3.2 and the effect of theta.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Gentle entry with very high bluntness to give a low-heat-flux front point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Establishes a low-q, moderate-T corner and tests geometry validity at b=1.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: only gamma changes to -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":423000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cleanly separates the gamma effect on T, q and g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: only bluntness changes to 1.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the bluntness effect on q and T and checks geometry validity at b=1.1.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: only diameter changes to 3.15.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the diameter effect and the mass-fraction margin near its limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Lower cone angle (58 deg) with moderate bluntness, to learn the theta effect on Cd, q and mass.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.75,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":58.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":375000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the theta effect at moderate bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Deliberately steep gamma=-4.2 on a large blunt design to locate the g boundary.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-4.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":303000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":376,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds how far gamma can go at large D and high theta before max_g fails. If g stays below 12, T falls further.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate step between the moderate and aggressive designs: b=1.15, gamma=-3.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":316000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":386,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely feasible candidate near the g limit with low T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the geometry boundary with b=1.3 at theta=69.9, where the bluntness index is about 0.85.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the validity boundary for very blunt noses and, if valid, gives a low-q point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"theta=62 with b=0.9 is a safe geometry that examines the cone-angle trend at higher bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":340000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shows whether high theta is truly needed or only enables higher bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-954afbe3d7da\",\"rationale\":\"Start from the low-bluntness C-954afbe3d7da and raise b to 1.0 with larger D and gamma=-3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":309000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests transfer of the trend to a second parent at theta=66.3.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-cone angle 45 deg with b=0.6 gives geometric diversity and tests a weaker-Cd design.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":45.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":460000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks how much worse a moderate theta is, to confirm the high-theta strategy.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Test the mass-fraction limit with D=3.3 at b=1.2 and gamma=-3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":382,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the diameter ceiling from the mass-fraction constraint. If feasible, the lowest q and T both improve.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Small-diameter blunt design at gamma=-3.4 for coverage of the trade-off at higher heat flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.4,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":420000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the diameter scaling at high bluntness and whether smaller D degrades g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-924ebfff660f\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate design at theta=68, b=1.0, D=3.05 and gamma=-3.4, a balanced point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.05,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":321000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives an intermediate point between the aggressive and safe designs and checks the g margin at gamma=-3.4.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":191750,"type":"result","duration_ms":241062,"uuid":"0e6f6cb9-5fa3-4d3a-ad96-56a8ad73fb31","ttft_stream_ms":1437,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":1437,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
